  plain_english: 'A vineyard designation names the specific vineyard where the grapes grew. Labels might say something like "Martha\'s Vineyard" or "To Kalon Vineyard." This is a more specific claim than an AVA or appellation; it identifies one particular piece of land. At least 95% of the wine must come from grapes grown in that specific vineyard. Vineyard designations are premium indicators because they suggest terroir specificity and a winemaker\'s belief that the site produces grapes distinctive enough to merit individual recognition. Wines with vineyard designations typically command higher prices than their appellation-level counterparts.',
