    { q: 'Why does the 14% ABV threshold matter?', a: 'Wines above 14% ABV have different labeling requirements (must declare specific ABV) and higher federal excise tax rates. This threshold influences winemaking decisions, as some producers aim to keep wines just under 14% for tax and labeling advantages.' }
